<article class="env-theorem" id="BDB1F7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/BDB1F7">Theorem <span data-tag="BDB1F7">1.1.5.13</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a topological category, and let $X, Y \in \calC $ be objects. Then the counit map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[ |\bHom _{\sCoNerve [\tNerve (\calC )]}(X,Y)| \rightarrow \bHom _{\calC }(X,Y) \]
</div>
  <p> is a weak homotopy equivalence of topological spaces. </p>
</article>